SAUCEDECK bench 2026-10-22 (production firmware 414e25d, branch feature/keymap-wifi-helper)

== Chip ==
esptool flash_id (after 1200 bps touch): ESP32-S3 (QFN56) rev v0.2, embedded 4 MB flash (XMC),
embedded 2 MB PSRAM (AP_3v3) -> ESP32-S3FH4R2. Partition -> huge_app.csv (fw 1.21 MB).

== Wi-Fi portal (Task 16 / spike A open items) ==
Operator: two-knob 5 s hold -> deck joined home Wi-Fi (saved credentials).
Mac: dns-sd saucedeck.local -> 10.0.0.88. curl http://saucedeck.local/param -> HTTP 200, 6072 B,
24 fields t1..t12 / v1..v12 pre-filled with current map (key/f13..). -> custom params in STA web
portal + mDNS: PASS.

== LED key feedback (2953ba0) ==
Operator: keys work with the new pattern (key N -> N LEDs, rainbow). PASS (Wi-Fi off).

== Wi-Fi reachability ==
After reflash + 5 s hold, screen said "saucedeck.local" but Mac: ping 10.0.0.88 0/3, HTTP 000,
/24 ping sweep found no deck MAC (28:84:85:69:2a:0c) beyond a stale ARP entry, no mDNS answer.
-> banner showed a stale "joined" state. Fixed in a1aab3c (live WiFi.status, IP/RSSI banner).
Pending: operator reads the new banner.
New banner (a1aab3c): "10.0.0.8 -76dBm" -> deck really joined (DHCP gave .8, the .88 seen before was stale).
Operator's device: page reachable ("I can see it") -> deck Wi-Fi + web portal PASS.
This Mac (en0 Ethernet 10.0.0.74 + en1 Wi-Fi 10.0.0.109, 5 GHz): ping 0/3, HTTP timeout on both
interfaces, ARP for .8 "(incomplete)" -> deck never answers the Mac at L2. Earlier .88 session did
answer over en1. Likely AP client/band isolation between 5 GHz and 2.4 GHz clients [unverified].
RSSI -76 dBm at 11 dBm TX: usable, weak; watch for drops.
